<article class="env-lemma" id="0AC6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AC6">Lemma <span data-tag="0AC6">68.18.4</span>.</a> In diagram (<a href="/tag/0AC1" data-tag="0AC1">68.18.0.1</a>) the set (<a href="/tag/0AC2" data-tag="0AC2">68.18.0.2</a>) is finite if $f$ is of finite type and $f$ is quasi-finite at $x$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The morphism $q$ is quasi-finite at every $w \in F_{x, z}$, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ABM" data-tag="0ABM">67.27.2</a>. Hence the lemma follows from Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ABN" data-tag="0ABN">67.27.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>